CHAPTER VI
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 43
(1) The community may participate in the implementation of protection for women and children victims of acts of violence.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes among others:
a. establishing family partners at the kalurahan level;
b. establishing community institutions whose field of work is in the protection of women and children;
c. conducting independent socialization of the rights of women and children;
d. undertaking preventive measures if indications of violence against women and children are found in the community;
e. providing first aid to women and children victims of violence; and
f. reporting to the competent authorities if violence against women and children occurs in their environment.
(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by individuals, community institutions, educational institutions, religious institutions, and the business sector.

